# WhyEV Backend — environment variables (MVP)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HOW TO USE:
#   1. Copy this file:  cp .env.example .env
#   2. Fill in every value marked with  ← GET THIS
#   3. Never commit .env to git (it's in .gitignore already)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 1. APP BASICS
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Which mode the app runs in.
# development → shows /docs page, full error details, SQL logs
# production  → hides errors from users, disables /docs
ENVIRONMENT=development

# When true, FastAPI hot-reloads on file save and prints SQL queries.
# Set to false in production.
DEBUG=true

# Master app secret. Used to sign cookies and derive internal secrets.
# HOW TO GENERATE:
#   Open terminal → python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
#   Paste the output here.
SECRET_KEY=←paste-output-of-secrets.token_hex(32)-here

# Which frontend URLs can call the API (browser security).
# Add your deployed frontend URL when you go live.
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:5173


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 2. DATABASE — Supabase (free tier works great for MVP)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# STEP-BY-STEP:
#   1. Go to  supabase.com  → New Project
#   2. Pick a name (e.g. "whyev"), set a strong DB password, choose region
#      (ap-south-1 = Mumbai is closest to India)
#   3. Wait ~2 min for project to spin up
#   4. Left sidebar → Project Settings → Database
#   5. Scroll to "Connection string" → select "URI" tab
#   6. Copy the string that looks like:
#      postgresql://postgres:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@db.xxxx.supabase.co:5432/postgres
#   7. Change "postgresql://" to "postgresql+asyncpg://"  (required for async)
#   8. Paste below
#
# NOTE: Supabase also enables pgvector automatically — no extra setup needed.
#
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://postgres:YOUR-DB-PASSWORD@db.XXXX.supabase.co:5432/postgres


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 3. JWT — Login Token Secrets
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# JWT_SECRET signs your login tokens. Anyone with this string can fake a login
# for any user — keep it secret and different from SECRET_KEY above.
#
# HOW TO GENERATE:
#   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
#   (run again for a fresh value, different from SECRET_KEY)
#
JWT_SECRET=←paste-a-different-secrets.token_hex(32)-here

# Access token lifetime. 900 seconds = 15 minutes.
# After this, the frontend must use the refresh token to get a new one.
JWT_ACCESS_TTL=900

# Refresh token lifetime. 2592000 seconds = 30 days.
# After this, the user must sign in with Google again.
JWT_REFRESH_TTL=2592000


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 4. GOOGLE OAUTH — "Sign in with Google"
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# STEP-BY-STEP:
#   1. Go to  console.cloud.google.com
#   2. Create a new project (or reuse one) — top-left dropdown → New Project
#   3. Left menu → APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen
#      - User type: External → Create
#      - App name: WhyEV | Support email: your email
#      - Add scope: .../auth/userinfo.email and .../auth/userinfo.profile
#      - Save and Continue (skip test users for now)
#   4. Left menu → APIs & Services → Credentials
#      → Create Credentials → OAuth 2.0 Client ID
#      - Application type: Web application
#      - Name: WhyEV Backend
#      - Authorised JavaScript origins:
#          http://localhost:3000   (your frontend dev URL)
#      - Authorised redirect URIs:
#          http://localhost:3000/auth/callback   (adjust to your frontend route)
#      → Create
#   5. A popup shows your Client ID and Client Secret — copy both below.
#
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=←your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=←your-client-secret


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 5. GROQ API KEY POOL — Free Open-Source LLMs (Llama 3)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# WHY MULTIPLE KEYS?
#   Free Groq tier = 14,400 requests/day AND 6,000 tokens/min per key.
#   With 3 keys: ~43,000 req/day and the pool auto-rotates when one hits the limit.
#
# HOW TO CREATE MULTIPLE FREE ACCOUNTS (Gmail + trick):
#   Gmail ignores dots and allows "+" aliases — they all land in YOUR inbox.
#   So  yourname@gmail.com  is the same as  your.name+whyev1@gmail.com
#
#   Account 1: yourname+whyev1@gmail.com
#   Account 2: yourname+whyev2@gmail.com
#   Account 3: yourname+whyev3@gmail.com
#
# FOR EACH ACCOUNT:
#   1. Go to  console.groq.com
#   2. Click "Sign Up" → sign in with that Gmail alias
#   3. Left sidebar → API Keys → Create API Key
#   4. Name it "whyev-key-1" (or any name)
#   5. Copy the  gsk_...  value — it's only shown ONCE
#   6. Paste into GROQ_API_KEY_1, GROQ_API_KEY_2, etc. below
#
# The pool (app/core/groq_pool.py) auto-rotates across all filled keys.
# Leave unused keys empty — the pool ignores blank values.
#
GROQ_API_KEY_1=gsk_←your-first-groq-key
GROQ_API_KEY_2=gsk_←your-second-groq-key
GROQ_API_KEY_3=gsk_←your-third-groq-key
GROQ_API_KEY_4=
GROQ_API_KEY_5=
GROQ_API_KEY_6=
GROQ_API_KEY_7=
GROQ_API_KEY_8=
GROQ_API_KEY_9=
GROQ_API_KEY_10=

# Which models to use (don't change unless Groq removes them)
# Full list: console.groq.com/docs/models
LLM_AGENT_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
LLM_CLASSIFIER_MODEL=llama-3.1-8b-instant


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 6. SENTRY — Error Monitoring (optional for MVP, strongly recommended)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Sentry catches crashes and sends you an email/Slack alert with the full
# stack trace. Free tier = 5,000 errors/month.
#
# STEP-BY-STEP:
#   1. Go to  sentry.io → Sign Up (free)
#   2. Create a new project → Platform: FastAPI (or Python)
#   3. Project name: whyev-backend
#   4. Copy the DSN — looks like: https://abc123@o123.ingest.sentry.io/456
#   5. Paste below
#
# Leave empty to disable Sentry entirely.
#
SENTRY_DSN=
